PROJECT
DentaPulse is a multi-tenant dental practice management SaaS: (A) EMR with an interactive SVG odontogram, treatment plans and payments; (B) consumable inventory with automatic, transactional deduction per procedure "recipe"; (C) URL-based personalized public demo and patient self-booking.

STACK
pnpm monorepo:
- apps/web: Next.js (App Router), TypeScript strict, Tailwind, shadcn/ui (Radix), lucide-react, TanStack Query.
- apps/api: Node 20, Express, TypeScript, Mongoose, zod, pino. Deployed to Vercel as serverless Functions.
- packages/shared: zod schemas, inferred types, constants (FDI teeth, enums) used by BOTH apps.
- MongoDB Atlas (managed replica set; multi-document transactions are required). NO Docker anywhere in this project: no Dockerfiles, no docker-compose. Local dev connects to an Atlas dev database.

ENGINEERING RULES
1. TypeScript strict. No `any`. No unused exports.
2. Multi-tenancy: every tenant-owned document has clinicId. clinicId is ALWAYS read from the authenticated JWT, never from body/params/query. Every query filters by clinicId.
3. Validate every request (body, params, query) with zod schemas from packages/shared.
4. Controllers are thin. Business logic lives in services. Services own DB access.
5. Money is stored as integers. Default currency is DZD, stored as whole dinars (no centimes). Format only through the shared formatDA/formatMoney helpers.
6. Inventory changes happen ONLY through atomic conditional updates inside a transaction, and always write a StockMovement row.
7. Errors: a typed AppError with a machine-readable code and HTTP status; one central error handler; never leak stack traces.
8. Tests: Vitest (unit + integration using mongodb-memory-server in replica-set mode), Playwright for e2e.
9. Conventional commits. After each task, summarize files changed and how to run and test them.

SERVERLESS RULES (deployment target: Vercel, two projects: web and api)
10. No in-memory state that matters: no module-level caches for business data, no in-memory rate limiters or lockouts.
11. No local disk writes. Files go to object storage.
12. No setInterval, node-cron or background loops. Scheduled work is an HTTP endpoint protected by CRON_SECRET and triggered by Vercel Cron; every scheduled handler must be idempotent (Vercel Cron delivery is best-effort, so missed or duplicate runs happen).
13. Cache the Mongo connection on globalThis, keep maxPoolSize small, never connect at import time, never disconnect per request.
14. Keep each request short. Transactions must be brief and contain only DB operations (no network calls, PDF generation or emails inside a transaction).
15. Every function has an explicit maxDuration; long work is chunked or split.

DESIGN SYSTEM ("Modern Clinical Slate")
- Canvas zinc-50, cards white with 1px zinc-200 border, rounded-xl, no heavy shadows.
- Primary teal-700 (#0F766E). Active tooth highlight indigo-700 (#4338CA).
- Status pills: emerald-50/emerald-700 (in stock, confirmed), amber-50/amber-700 (low, pending), rose-50/rose-700 (out, cancelled).
- Font: Inter or Plus Jakarta Sans via next/font. Use tabular-nums for currency, stock counts and FDI tooth numbers.
- Quick tasks (add patient, tooth history, adjust stock) open in a right-side Sheet, not a new page.
- Zero layout shift: reserve space for anything that loads or changes.
- Accessibility: keyboard navigable, visible focus rings, aria labels, WCAG AA contrast.

LOCALISATION RULES (target market: Algeria, product language: French)
16. All user-visible text is FRENCH (formal "vous", sentence case, no anglicisms): interface, validation and error messages, toasts, PDFs, emails, WhatsApp/SMS templates, demo banner. Identifiers (code, DB fields, enum values, API routes) stay in English.
17. No hardcoded UI strings. Use next-intl message catalogs (apps/web/messages/fr.json), default locale "fr". The API returns stable machine-readable error codes and the web app maps them to French messages. API-generated text (PDFs, reminder templates) uses catalogs in packages/shared.
18. Formats: dates dd/MM/yyyy, 24-hour time (14:30), space as thousands separator, comma as decimal separator, currency shown as "12 500 DA". Always use the shared formatters (formatDate, formatTime, formatDA); never call Intl inline.
19. Defaults: country DZ, phone prefix +213, timezone Africa/Algiers, locale fr-DZ, Friday closed (Saturday configurable). All configurable per clinic.
20. Use Tailwind logical utilities (ms-, me-, ps-, pe-, start-, end-) from day one so Arabic/RTL can be added later without rewrites.
21. Follow docs/GLOSSAIRE.fr.md for every term.
